    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50785" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vexātor</span></b> , ōris,
			m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				troubler</i>, <i>harasser</i>, <i>abuser</i>, <i>vexer</i> (Ciceron.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">custosne urbis an direptor et vexator esset
					Antonius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 3, 11, 27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aetatulae suae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Sest. 8, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">furoris (Clodii),</span>”
				i. e. <i>opposer</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Mil. 13, 35</span></i>
			.</div>
